    29	#     - variant: if the path passes through (5,5) on a "\" segment and there is a magenta at (6,4),
    30	#       then the magenta at (6,4) is the splitter. The emitted slash ray starts from (6,4), so one
    31	#       branch immediately meets the blue path at (5,5) and then continues beyond it without overwrite.
    32	#     - difference: solver must inspect side-neighbor cells of the segment interior, not just cells on
    33	#       the segment itself.
    34	#   complexity_calibration:
    35	#     - adjacency is restricted to exactly one perpendicular-diagonal step. This is visibly different
